<DocsLayout
  title="Sync — Quakboard Docs"
  heading="Sync"
  summary="Share history and snippets across your devices with end-to-end encryption. Sync is opt-in, off by default, and designed so we can never read your clipboard."
>
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    When you enable sync, Quakboard generates an encryption key derived from
    your passphrase and stored only on your devices. Every item is <strong
      >encrypted on the device before it's uploaded</strong
    >. Our relay sees nothing but opaque ciphertext and the timing of changes —
    never content, never plaintext.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each device decrypts incoming changes locally and merges them into its own
    history. There is no master copy on a server you can be locked out of — every
    device holds a full, usable database on its own.
  </p>

  <h2>Turn it on</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <code>Settings → Sync</code> and choose <strong>Enable sync</strong>.</li>
    <li>
      Set a sync passphrase. This is the only thing that can decrypt your data —
      we don't store it and <strong>can't recover it</strong>, so keep it
      somewhere safe.
    </li>
    <li>
      On your second device, install Quakboard, open <code>Settings → Sync</code
      >, and enter the same passphrase. History begins merging within seconds.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What syncs — and what doesn't</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Synced:</strong> text, links, colors, code, and pinned snippets.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Synced (optional):</strong> images and files, with a per-item size
      cap you control. Off by default to keep transfers small.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Never synced:</strong> items you mark <em>local-only</em>, and
      anything captured while <a href="/docs/privacy">incognito copy</a> is
      active.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Conflicts and ordering</h2>
  <p>
    History is an append-only log keyed by capture time, so merges are
    conflict-free — items from every device interleave by when they were copied.
    For snippets you edit (like a renamed signature), the most recent edit wins,
    and the previous version is kept for 30 days in case you need it back.
  </p>

  <h2>Selective and paused sync</h2>
  <p>
    You can pause sync at any time from the menu bar without losing local
    history, or set a device to <strong>receive only</strong> so it pulls
    snippets from your other machines without pushing its own clipboard up. This
    is handy for a shared or work computer.
  </p>

  <h2>Self-hosting the relay</h2>
  <p>
    Because the relay only ever handles ciphertext, you can point Quakboard at
    your own server under <code>Settings → Sync → Advanced</code>. The protocol
    is documented and the relay is open source. Whether you use ours or your
    own, the encryption story is identical.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
